#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""nemesis — repo malware / supply-chain threat scanner for macOS & Linux.

Defensive tool. Scans a directory tree — or a remote GitHub repo it fetches
itself (``nemesis scan owner/repo`` / a git URL) — for the patterns attackers
plant in source so that ``git clone && install`` ships a backdoor: pipe-to-shell
droppers, reverse shells, crypto miners, obfuscated/dynamic-exec payloads,
persistence hooks (cron/systemd/launchd), credential & data exfiltration,
malicious package-manager lifecycle scripts, embedded executables, destructive
commands and known-bad file hashes. For GitHub specifically it also flags
poisoned CI (GitHub Actions pwn-requests, script injection, unpinned actions),
weaponized git config/submodules (core.fsmonitor, ext:: transport, !-aliases),
and review-evasion via hidden Unicode (Trojan Source bidi / zero-width).

The remote target is fetched read-only (shallow clone with submodule recursion
and ext::/file:: transports disabled and hooks neutralised, or a stdlib codeload
tarball) into a temp dir, scanned, then deleted — repo code is never executed.

Detection is signature + heuristic. No scanner catches *everything*; treat a
clean result as "no known patterns matched", not "provably safe". Conversely,
heuristics can false-positive on security tooling and test fixtures — review
findings before trusting --fix on a tree you do not control.

Remediation (--fix) is conservative and reversible:
  * neutralize  -> comment out / strip the offending line(s), keep a .bak
  * quarantine  -> gzip-move the whole file into a quarantine vault + manifest
  * report      -> record only
Default is dry-run: nothing is modified without --fix.

Stdlib only. Runs on stock Python 3.8+ shipped with macOS and Linux.

Signatures come from two places: built-in regex/heuristics, and an optional local
signature DB seeded from real feeds via ``nemesis update`` (ClamAV hash sigs +
.ndb body-pattern signatures compiled to an in-process byte matcher — no
key needed; abuse.ch MalwareBazaar/ThreatFox hashes + URL/domain/IP IOCs — free
Auth-Key from https://auth.abuse.ch/). Save the key once with ``nemesis auth`` and
it is auto-loaded every run; precedence is env NEMESIS_ABUSECH_AUTHKEY >
~/.nemesis/config.json > the _HARDCODED_AUTHKEY constant below. ``scan`` never
touches the network; it only loads the cached DB, so it runs fully offline once
seeded.

Usage:
  ./nemesis auth --key KEY                    # save abuse.ch key (chmod 600 config)
  ./nemesis auth --key KEY --shell-rc         # also export from .zprofile/.bashrc
  ./nemesis update                            # fetch enabled feeds (hashes/IOC/OSV) into ~/.nemesis/db
  ./nemesis update --feed osv                  # dependency-CVE advisories (PyPI+npm) for SCA
  ./nemesis update --all                      # also opt-in feeds (clamav-main, mb-full)
  ./nemesis update --list                     # show feeds, license, freshness
  ./nemesis                                   # interactive: browse, pick, scan, decide
  ./nemesis ui [DIR]                          # same, starting at DIR
  ./nemesis scan PATH [options]
  ./nemesis scan PATH --interactive           # decide per threat: neutralize/quarantine/erase/ignore
  ./nemesis scan owner/repo                   # fetch + scan a GitHub repo
  ./nemesis scan gitlab:owner/repo            # also gitlab: / codeberg: / bitbucket:
  ./nemesis scan https://github.com/o/r.git --ref main
  ./nemesis scan https://host/path/installer.sh    # direct file URL: download + scan, never run
  ./nemesis scan . --json report.json
  ./nemesis scan ~/Downloads/somerepo --fix
  ./nemesis scan PATH --no-feeds             # regex+heuristics only, no DB
  ./nemesis scan pkg.tar.gz                   # scan inside an archive (zip/tar/rar/7z)
  ./nemesis scan pkg.rar --disinfect --out clean/   # fix solvable threats, write clean copy
  ./nemesis gate pkg.tar.gz                   # JSON verdict + exit 0/10/20/2 (for other tools)
  cat installer.sh | ./nemesis gate -         # scan text piped on stdin
  ./nemesis ignore --list                     # findings you accepted ([i]gnore)
  ./nemesis restore QUARANTINE_ID --quarantine-dir VAULT   # undo a quarantine
  ./nemesis restore --quarantine-dir VAULT --list          # see the vault
  ./nemesis selftest                         # verify the engine works

Archives: zip/tar(.gz/.bz2/.xz) are scanned in-stream (nothing written to disk).
rar/7z stream in-process via libarchive when present (no external CLI); otherwise
they fall back to a sandboxed extract. --sandbox extract / --disinfect decompress
into a temp dir that is ALWAYS erased after the scan (clean or not); only
--out/--keep-extract retains a result. --password / --password-file scan encrypted
members you legitimately hold; unscannable archives stay fail-closed.

Exit codes (scan): 0 clean · 1 findings (warn tier) · 3 blocking threats · 2 error.
Exit codes (gate): 0 allow · 10 warn · 20 block · 2 error (fail-closed).
"""
